    {
      "id": "8f1ghyn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Characteristics of Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plant cell walls are composed of cellulose, distinguishing them from animal cells.",
        "Plant tissues are classified into dividing Meristematic Tissues and specialized Permanent Tissues.",
        "Photosynthesis converts carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen using light energy in chloroplasts.",
        "Vascular tissues include Xylem (water transport) and Phloem (food transport).",
        "Plant growth and responses are regulated by key hormones like Auxin, Gibberellin, Cytokinin, Ethylene, and Abscisic Acid."
      ],
      "id": "4ki4nmo"
    },
